         The Town Clerk’s Office hours:  Mon - Fri 8:30am - 4:30pm  Open until 8:00pm on the 1st and 3rd Tuesdays Sept-June  Closed on Fridays in July and August Business certificates   – all owners must be present to sign the form at the Town Clerk’s Office, unless the signatures are notarized, and then the form can be mailed to our office. • Information and questions about business certificates •  Business Certificate Application Use the above link to create an account to apply on-line. •  Statement of Change Dog Licensing A current rabies certificate must be on file with the Clerks Office. Late fees applied automatically  starting May 1st  (late fee $25.00). PLEASE NOTE:  "Service Animal" is defined as dogs that are individually trained to do work or perform tasks for people with  disabilities .  Emotional support dogs are  not  included in this definition. Marriages NOTICE:  Effective August 1, 2023, marriage intentions are by appointment only.  Please call the Town Clerk's Office to make an appointment.  781-871-1874 x 1002 Applying for a  Marriage License  (to be married) – You and your future spouse must appear in person to sign the required forms. The 3-day waiting period to obtain the license begins once all materials and payment have been finalized. Licenses are valid for 60 days.  The last available appointment is 3:30 p.m. unless of course you come in on the 1st or 3rd Tuesday, then it is 7:00 p.m. You’ll need to provide:     Original birth certificate, and driver's license or passport  your Social Security number       $30.00 (which includes a certified copy) The name you’ll use after the wedding if you’ve decided to change it Original Divorce Decree(s) if previously married Original documents will be returned. •  Certified Copy of your Marriage  – see Vital Records section •  Marriage Ceremonies  –  C URRENTLY UNAVAILABLE   Notary Services  – A notary does NOT view the documents and its contents or give legal advice - they simply witness a signature. Any document to be notarized must contain the appropriate notarial certificate on it already, should not require additional witnesses and must not already be signed.  Oath of Office  –  if you have been appointed to a board or committee and have not taken your oath of office, please email  clerkdept@rockland-ma.gov  to make an appointment & for instructions. Zoning / ZBA Appeals  – •  Filing Applications  –  this should be done through Zoning Coordinator •  No Appeal Decisions  –  decisions that have not been appealed will be available 21 business day later. You must provide the Building Department with a copy of the receipt after filing with the Registry of Deeds. •  Filing an Appeal  –  A copy of an appeal can be submitted at the clerk’s office .  Our office will print and date/time stamp the appeal. Public Records Requests   -  The public records law allows for 10 business days and in some cases a 15-day extension to provide a response for the requested records.  Vital Records Online Ordering – be sure our office has your record before ordering – see notes below Birth Certificate  –   Rockland will only have your record if you were born in Rockland or your parents were living here at the time of your birth. We will not have your record if you were born outside of Massachusetts. Death Certificate  – Rockland will only have this record if the deceased passed away in Rockland or they were on record as living here at the time of their death. We will not have this record if they passed away outside of Massachusetts Marriage Certificates  – we encourage you to email clerkdept@rockland-ma.gov before ordering marriage certificates online to ensure Rockland has your record. Rockland will only have your record if you filed your intentions to be married here.  
     

 
